{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310524,"nonce":"OMr/i5ew3Gsx9GQNayBJQtPjuYA=","title":"`var c = anonExpr.field` where the field's declared type is itself an anonymous shape lost the inner shape — reads on `c` returned null ...","message":"FIXED in `tast/ast_lowering.rs::infer_expression_type` FieldAccess arm: reads field type from the receiver's Anonymous shape directly (walking TypeAlias chains so typedefs participate). Only falls back to the symbol-table path for non-anon receivers. Original repros (kept for reference):\n\n```haxe\nvar p = { a: 10, b: 20 };\nvar q = { child: p };\nvar c = q.child;          // c's inferred type is too narrow\ntrace(\"c.a=\" + c.a);      // prints \"c.a=null\"\n\n// Or in a chain:\ntrace(q.child.a);         // null\n```\n\n`c == p` returns `false` — the pointer value extracted from `q.child` is non-null but reading `c.a` returns null. Adding an explicit `:{a:Int,b:Int}` annotation at the binding site (or `:Inner` typedef) makes everything work.\n\nRoot cause hypothesis: when the outer anon literal `{ child: p }` is constructed, the outer's \"child\" field type is registered as a placeholder/empty anon rather than the value's actual anon shape. Subsequent reads use the placeholder shape, which has no \"a\" entry, so the runtime returns null from `rayzor_anon_get_field_by_index`. The TAST/HIR pass that infers the outer literal's field types must propagate the inner literal's complete shape (not just acknowledge it's an anon).\n\nSame root as [[bugs-cross-function-anon-return-inference]] (no separate file yet) — `var loaded = ld.load()` where `load():LoadedModel` returns a typedef-wrapped anon. Without an explicit `:LoadedModel`, `loaded`'s field types collapse and reads return null. Workaround: annotate the binding site.\n\nHow to apply: until fixed, anon-of-anon construction sites need explicit binding annotations. Don't `var x = call()` if the result type is an anon-of-anon — write `var x:T = call()`.\n\nDistinct from [[bugs-anon-setter-value-escape]] (use-after-free in InsertFreePass) — that one was fixed; this one is type inference dropping shape information.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_anon_field_type_inference_loss` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}